openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: FuzeFront Portal API
  version: 1.4.0
  description: >-
    **⚠️ SUPERSEDED (FF-EPIC-17-S7).** The standalone-`portals`-table model this
    contract froze — including the master-admin CRUD (`/api/v1/admin/portals`)
    and its generated `@fuzefront/portal-client` — is SUPERSEDED by portal CRUD
    expressed as ORG-TREE operations in the Security API
    (`packages/security/openapi.yaml`, tag `portals`, `@fuzefront/security-client`
    ≥ 0.7.0). A "portal" is now an `organizations` row whose `parentOrgId` is the
    platform root, carrying a portal-root + tenant attributes — NOT a separate
    `portals` entity. New work MUST target the org-tree endpoints. This file is
    retained for reference during the backend migration and for the still-live
    surfaces (`GET /api/v1/portal/context`, `GET /api/v1/portal/current`) until
    those are reconciled too; `@fuzefront/portal-client` should be **retired**
    once the fan-out moves off it. Retirement, the tenant-attribute storage
    decision (recommended: an `organizations`-keyed extension table), and the
    `portals.id → organizations.id` FK-retargets (FF-EPIC-11/12/13/15/16) are an
    owner/orchestrator decision + migration follow-up, tracked in the
    FF-EPIC-17-S7 contract PR — not executed here.


    REST API for **multi-tenant portals** — the first-class `portals` object that
    lets one shared FuzeFront deployment serve many isolated white-label tenant
    portals. This contract freezes two surfaces:

      1. **Public portal context** (`GET /api/v1/portal/context`) — the
         unauthenticated boot endpoint the shell/login call to resolve the active
         portal (id, slug, branding, identity policy, auth entry points) for the
         current Host. Renders *before* login (a branded login screen), so it
         exposes only public branding/identity-policy/auth-entry data — never a
         raw `portals` row. Source: FF-EPIC-10-S2.

      2. **Master-admin portal CRUD** (`/api/v1/admin/portals`) — create / list /
         get / update / suspend / resume, Permit **platform-admin** gated and
         fail-closed (non-admin ⇒ 403). This surfaces the resumable provisioning
         pipeline behind a versioned, generated client. Source: FF-EPIC-09-S3.

    A portal's own self-scoped identity (`GET /api/v1/portal/current`) is also
    frozen here so the portal-admin console can read the caller's own portal
    (resolved from the session, never from a client-supplied id).

    This file is the single source of truth for `@fuzefront/portal-client`.
    Changing the API means amending this file first (see the `api-contract-first`
    skill), bumping `info.version` + the changelog, re-linting (Spectral), then
    regenerating the client (`openapi-typescript`). UI, backend, and tests import
    the SAME generated types, so drift becomes a compile error.

    ### Fail-closed semantics (contract, not decoration)
      * A **suspended** portal fails closed — `403 PORTAL_SUSPENDED`.
      * The **root** portal (slug `fuzefront`) cannot be suspended —
        `409 ROOT_PORTAL_PROTECTED`.
      * Creating a portal with a duplicate slug — `409 SLUG_TAKEN`.
      * A non-platform-admin caller on any admin route — `403 FORBIDDEN`
        (an authorization denial, NOT a sign-in redirect; only `401`
        re-authenticates).
      * A caller acting on a portal they do not administer — `403 FORBIDDEN_PORTAL`,
        with zero cross-tenant data leaked.

    All portal capability is staged behind the master feature flag
    `fuzefront.platform.multi-tenant-portals` (default OFF, FF-EPIC-09-S4); authz
    stays in Permit — the flag is rollout convenience only.

    The master-admin fleet list's `identityMode`/`launchUrl` fields (Portals
    Directory, backend slice S1) are separately staged behind
    `fuzefront.platform.portals-directory` (default OFF) — when OFF,
    `GET /api/v1/admin/portals` omits both fields entirely (not `null`).
    Backend slice S5 adds the read-vs-manage refinement on the SAME flag:
    when ON, the blanket admin-only gate on `GET /api/v1/admin/portals` is
    replaced by a per-portal Permit `read`/`manage` check (`canManage`,
    `canOpen` — both OPTIONAL, same gating), and `launchUrl` is only present
    on rows the caller may launch (`canOpen: true`). When OFF, S5 changes
    nothing — the route stays admin-role gated exactly as before.
  license:
    name: UNLICENSED

x-superseded-by:
  by: packages/security/openapi.yaml
  client: '@fuzefront/security-client'
  since: FF-EPIC-17-S7
  reason: >-
    Portal CRUD is reconciled onto the unified organizations+parent_id org tree
    (tag `portals`). The standalone `portals`-table model and
    `@fuzefront/portal-client` are superseded; `GET /api/v1/admin/portals` is
    replaced by `GET /api/v1/security/portals`. Retirement of this client and
    the `portals.id → organizations.id` FK-retargets are a migration follow-up,
    not executed in the contract PR.

servers:
  - url: '{baseUrl}'
    description: >-
      Platform backend serving the portal surface. Paths below are absolute
      (`/api/v1/...`) and match exactly what the shell and admin consoles bind to.
      The frontend calls these on a same-origin base — never a cross-origin host.
    variables:
      baseUrl:
        default: http://fuzefront-backend:3001
        description: Cluster-internal base URL of the platform backend.

tags:
  - name: portal-context
    description: Public, pre-auth portal resolution for the shell/login boot.
  - name: portal-self
    description: The caller's own portal, resolved from the session.
  - name: admin-portals
    description: Master-admin portal lifecycle CRUD (Permit platform-admin gated).
  - name: health
    description: Service liveness / readiness.

security:
  - sessionAuth: []

paths:
  /api/v1/portal/context:
    get:
      operationId: getPortalContext
      tags: [portal-context]
      summary: Resolve the public context for the current portal
      description: >-
        Returns the active portal's public boot data (id, slug, branding,
        identity policy, auth entry points) for the Host/`/p/<slug>`/custom domain
        the request arrived on. **Unauthenticated** — it must render before login
        so a branded login screen can paint. Exposes only public
        branding/identity-policy/auth-entry fields; never a raw `portals` row.
        Fail-closed: an unknown host resolves to the root portal (for shell/UI
        routes), and a suspended portal returns 403 `PORTAL_SUSPENDED`.
      security: []
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The resolved portal context.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/PortalContext' }
        '403':
          description: The resolved portal is suspended (`PORTAL_SUSPENDED`).
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
        '404': { $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }

  /api/v1/portal/current:
    get:
      operationId: getCurrentPortal
      tags: [portal-self]
      summary: Get the caller's own portal
      x-pagination: exempt
      x-pagination-reason: >-
        Singleton — returns exactly one portal (the session-resolved portal the
        caller belongs to), never a growing collection.
      description: >-
        Returns the full portal record for the portal the authenticated caller
        belongs to, resolved from the session/token (`req.user.portalId`) — a
        `portalId` is **never** accepted from the client. Used by the portal-admin
        console to render portal identity (domain, owner, status). A caller acting
        on a portal they do not administer gets 403 `FORBIDDEN_PORTAL`.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The caller's portal.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Portal' }
        '401': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized' }
        '403': { $ref: '#/components/responses/ForbiddenPortal' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }

  /api/v1/admin/portals:
    get:
      operationId: listPortals
      tags: [admin-portals]
      summary: List portals (master-admin fleet view)
      description: >-
        Returns a cursor-paginated page of portals for the master-admin fleet
        list. A fresh install returns exactly one portal (the seeded root
        portal, slug `fuzefront`).

        When `fuzefront.platform.portals-directory` is OFF, this stays
        Permit **platform-admin** only — a non-admin caller is denied
        fail-closed with 403 `FORBIDDEN`, byte-identical to the pre-1.3.0
        contract.

        When the flag is ON (backend slice S5), the blanket admin-only gate
        is replaced by a per-portal Permit `read`/`manage` check on each
        portal's owning organization (`Organization:read` / `Organization:manage`,
        including the parent-org `org-admin` derivation for platform/master
        admins): a caller with `manage` on a portal's org sees it with
        `canManage: true, canOpen: true` and a `launchUrl`; a caller with
        only `read` sees it read-only (`canManage: false, canOpen: false`,
        no `launchUrl`); a portal the caller cannot even `read` is never
        returned (BOLA-safe filtering, never after-the-fact leakage). A
        caller with `read` authority over NONE of the portals this query
        would otherwise return still gets the fail-closed 403 `FORBIDDEN`
        no-access response — the read-vs-manage refinement only ever WIDENS
        who sees a 200 relative to the pre-flag blanket gate, never who is
        denied.
      parameters:
        - name: status
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Filter by lifecycle status. Omit for all statuses.
          schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/PortalStatus' }
        - name: q
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Free-text filter over name/slug/primary domain.
          schema: { type: string, maxLength: 200 }
        - name: limit
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Page size. Clamped to `maximum` server-side.
          schema: { type: integer, minimum: 1, maximum: 100, default: 25 }
        - name: cursor
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Opaque, server-issued pagination cursor (from `page.nextCursor`).
          schema: { type: string }
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of portals.
          content:
            application/json:
              # Inline `{ items, page }` envelope (structurally identical to
              # PortalPage) so the pagination gate — which does not resolve $ref —
              # sees the envelope. `components.schemas.PortalPage` is the named
              # alias the generated client exports.
              schema:
                type: object
                additionalProperties: false
                required: [items, page]
                properties:
                  items:
                    type: array
                    items: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Portal' }
                  page: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Page' }
        '401': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized' }
        '403': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }
    post:
      operationId: createPortal
      tags: [admin-portals]
      summary: Create (provision) a portal
      description: >-
        Provisions a new tenant portal via the resumable pipeline
        (org → Permit tenant → portal row → default subdomain → owner invite). The
        new portal starts `provisioned-pending-invite` (never silently `active`)
        and the owner invite dispatches with provisioning. `slug` is immutable and
        must be unique — a duplicate returns 409 `SLUG_TAKEN`. Permit
        **platform-admin** only.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/PortalCreate' }
      responses:
        '201':
          description: Portal created (status = provisioned-pending-invite).
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Portal' }
        '400': { $ref: '#/components/responses/ValidationError' }
        '401': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized' }
        '403': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden' }
        '409':
          description: A portal with this slug already exists (`SLUG_TAKEN`).
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }

  /api/v1/admin/portals/{portalId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PortalId'
    get:
      operationId: getPortal
      tags: [admin-portals]
      summary: Get a portal by id
      description: >-
        Returns the full portal record (branding, identity policy, billing mode,
        domains + verification/TLS status). Permit **platform-admin** only.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The portal.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Portal' }
        '401': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized' }
        '403': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden' }
        '404': { $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }
    patch:
      operationId: updatePortal
      tags: [admin-portals]
      summary: Update a portal (fields and/or lifecycle status)
      description: >-
        Partially updates a portal. `name`, `branding`, `identityPolicy`, and
        `billingMode` are mutable; `slug` is immutable and cannot be changed.
        Setting `status` is how the master-admin **suspends** (`active` →
        `suspended`) or **resumes** (`suspended` → `active`) a portal — this is
        the transition the fleet list and detail views bind to. Suspending the
        root portal (slug `fuzefront`) is refused with 409
        `ROOT_PORTAL_PROTECTED`. Permit **platform-admin** only. Equivalent
        semantic action endpoints are `POST .../suspend` and `POST .../resume`.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/PortalUpdate' }
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The updated portal.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Portal' }
        '400': { $ref: '#/components/responses/ValidationError' }
        '401': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized' }
        '403': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden' }
        '404': { $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound' }
        '409':
          description: >-
            The requested transition is refused — e.g. suspending the root portal
            (`ROOT_PORTAL_PROTECTED`).
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }

  /api/v1/admin/portals/{portalId}/suspend:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PortalId'
    post:
      operationId: suspendPortal
      tags: [admin-portals]
      summary: Suspend a portal
      description: >-
        Semantic lifecycle action equivalent to `PATCH .../{portalId}` with
        `{ "status": "suspended" }`. Flips the portal to `suspended`, after which
        it fails closed (paired with FF-EPIC-10 resolution: 403
        `PORTAL_SUSPENDED`) and any cached resolution is invalidated. Idempotent:
        suspending an already-suspended portal is a no-op 200. Suspending the root
        portal is refused with 409 `ROOT_PORTAL_PROTECTED`. Permit
        **platform-admin** only.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Portal suspended.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Portal' }
        '401': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized' }
        '403': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden' }
        '404': { $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound' }
        '409':
          description: The root portal cannot be suspended (`ROOT_PORTAL_PROTECTED`).
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }

  /api/v1/admin/portals/{portalId}/resume:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PortalId'
    post:
      operationId: resumePortal
      tags: [admin-portals]
      summary: Resume a suspended portal
      description: >-
        Semantic lifecycle action equivalent to `PATCH .../{portalId}` with
        `{ "status": "active" }`. Flips a `suspended` portal back to `active` and
        invalidates any cached resolution. Idempotent: resuming an already-active
        portal is a no-op 200. Permit **platform-admin** only.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Portal resumed (active).
          content:
            application/json:
              schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/Portal' }
        '401': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized' }
        '403': { $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden' }
        '404': { $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound' }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }

  /health:
    get:
      operationId: getHealth
      tags: [health]
      summary: Liveness / readiness
      description: Unauthenticated liveness/readiness probe for the portal surface.
      security: []
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Service healthy.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                additionalProperties: false
                required: [status]
                properties:
                  status: { type: string, enum: [ok] }
        '500': { $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError' }

components:
  securitySchemes:
    sessionAuth:
      type: http
      scheme: bearer
      description: >-
        Platform user session (Authentik OIDC bearer) carrying the `portal_id`
        claim. The backend authorizes admin routes via Permit's platform-admin
        role. Scope referenced in this contract: `portals:admin`.

  parameters:
    PortalId:
      name: portalId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: The portal's server-issued id (e.g. `prt_northwind`).
      schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/PortalId' }

  responses:
    Unauthorized:
      description: Missing or invalid session / token (re-authenticate).
      content:
        application/json:
          schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
    Forbidden:
      description: >-
        The caller is not a platform admin (`FORBIDDEN`). An authorization denial,
        never a sign-in redirect.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
    ForbiddenPortal:
      description: >-
        The caller acted on a portal they do not administer
        (`FORBIDDEN_PORTAL`) — no cross-tenant data is returned.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
    NotFound:
      description: Portal not found.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }
    ValidationError:
      description: Request body failed validation.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ValidationErrorBody' }
    InternalError:
      description: Unexpected server error.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorBody' }

  schemas:
    PortalId:
      type: string
      description: Server-issued portal id, immutable once provisioned.
      pattern: '^prt_[A-Za-z0-9]{1,40}$'
      examples: ['prt_fuzefront', 'prt_northwind']

    Slug:
      type: string
      description: >-
        URL-safe unique portal identifier used for `/p/<slug>` and the default
        subdomain, immutable once provisioned. The root portal's slug is
        `fuzefront`.
      pattern: '^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,38}[a-z0-9]$'
      examples: ['fuzefront', 'northwind']

    PortalStatus:
      type: string
      description: >-
        Lifecycle status. `provisioning` and `provisioned-pending-invite` are
