openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: FuzeFront Selection List Service API
  version: 1.0.0
  summary: Org-scoped, translatable selection lists (reference data) for the Fuze family.
  description: >-
    **FROZEN CONTRACT — FFRNT-187 (S1).** This file is the single source of truth
    for the `selection-list-service` HTTP surface and for the generated/derived
    client `@fuzeone/selection-list-client`. Nothing downstream (backend routes,
    migrations, UI, acceptance tests, docs) may diverge from it; a change to the
    API means amending **this file first**, bumping `info.version`, re-linting,
    and re-issuing the client (see the `api-contract-first` skill and
    `governance/`).


    ### What the service is

    A selection list is a named, org-scoped set of ordered, translatable choices
    (`countries`, `industries`, `ticket-priorities`, ...) that consuming
    applications render in dropdowns/pickers and persist by **item id**. The
    service owns three things and nothing else: the list/item structure, the
    per-locale translations of both, and the per-list access grants.


    ### The two identifiers, and why there are two

    Every item carries both an `id` and a `code`, and they are not
    interchangeable:

    * **`id`** — the service-minted, permanently immutable identifier consumers
      **persist** in their own rows. It is opaque and never displayed. Consumers
      store this and nothing else, which is what makes an item's label and its
      `code` safe to change later.
    * **`code`** — a human-meaningful interop key (`US`, `HIGH`) that is
      **immutable after create** and unique within its list. It exists for
      integrations that must map to an external system's vocabulary. It is a
      key, never a label: it is not translated and not shown to end users.

    Persisting a `code` instead of an `id` is the classic reference-data defect —
    it welds a display/interop concern to a foreign key. The contract makes the
    right choice the easy one: `POST /v1/resolve` takes ids.


    ### Archive is the default; purge is explicit

    Reference data is referenced. Deleting a row that thousands of consumer rows
    point at turns their stored id into a dangling reference, so the default
    destructive operation is **archive** (`status: archived`): the item stops
    being offered for new selections but still **resolves**, so existing rows
    keep rendering a real label. `DELETE` therefore archives unless the caller
    passes `?purge=true`, which is irreversible and permitted only to a
    `list-owner`. `POST /v1/resolve` deliberately resolves archived ids.


    ### Translations and the locale fallback

    List `name`/`description` and item `label`/`description` live in
    `*_translations` rows keyed by locale, never on the entity itself. Every
    representation of a list or an item therefore carries the resolved text plus
    `resolved_locale` (the locale the text actually came from) and `is_machine`
    (whether that text was machine-translated). The resolution order is fixed:

      1. the `locale` query parameter, if supplied and supported;
      2. the first supported language in the `Accept-Language` header;
      3. the list's `source_locale`;
      4. `en`.

    **A label is never `null`.** A missing translation falls through the chain
    rather than returning an empty string — a picker rendering blank rows is a
    worse failure than one rendering the source-locale text.

    `source_hash` on a translation row is the hash of the **source-locale** text
    the translation was produced from; when the source text changes the hash no
    longer matches and the translation is known-stale, which is what lets
    `POST /v1/selection-lists/{listId}/translations/{locale}/autofill` refresh
    only what actually drifted.


    ### Field casing

    Resource representations use `snake_case`, mirroring storage. The pagination
    envelope (`page.nextCursor`, `page.hasMore`, `page.total`) is `camelCase`
    because it is fixed verbatim by the family pagination standard
    (`governance/pagination-standard.md` §1) and is identical across every Fuze
    service. This split is intentional and load-bearing: the envelope is shared
    infrastructure, the payload is this service's own.


    ### Identifiers (governance/identifier-standard.md)

    Ids are **TypeID**-shaped — a registered type prefix, an underscore, and a
    UUIDv7 in base32 — minted exclusively by this service via `mintId()` from
    `@izzywdev/fuzefront-identity`. No create body accepts an `id`, and every
    create schema sets `additionalProperties: false`, so a client-supplied id
    cannot bind. On the wire ids are `type: string` and **opaque past the
    prefix**: validate the prefix, never parse further, never assume a length.

    | Entity | Prefix | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | selection list | `front_sl_` | `front_sl_01h455vb4pex5vsknk084sn02q` |
    | selection list item | `front_sli_` | `front_sli_01h455vb4pex5vsknk084sn02q` |

    Referenced spine ids keep their own prefixes (`org_`, `usr_`).

    **Registry note (S3 amendment):** prefixes `front_sl` and `front_sli` are
    registered in `packages/identity/src/registry.ts` (keys `selectionList` and
    `selectionListItem`). They are product-local types namespaced as `front_*`
    per the namespace gate (`gate_identifier.py --namespace`).


    ### Authorization

    Resource `SelectionList` in FuzeFront's Security API (backend/security's
    `/api/v1/security/authz/*`, called via `@fuzefront/auth`'s `AuthzClient`
    — this service embeds no policy-vendor SDK), with actions `read`,
    `add_value`, `update_value`, `remove_value`, `translate`, `update`,
    `delete`, `manage_access`. Grants are ReBAC resource-instance roles on the
    list instance, mirroring `Organization.roles['org-admin']` in
    `backend/src/permit/schema.ts`.

    | role | read | add_value | update_value | remove_value | translate | update | delete | manage_access |
    |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
    | `list-owner`       | x | x | x | x | x | x | x | x |
    | `list-editor`      | x | x | x | x | x | x |   |   |
    | `list-contributor` | x | x | x |   | x |   |   |   |
    | `list-translator`  | x |   |   |   | x |   |   |   |
    | `list-viewer`      | x |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |

    Each operation declares the action it requires in `x-permit-action`.
    **An id is never a capability** — knowing a list id grants nothing; every
    route re-checks the caller against the Security API, and a read the caller
    is not entitled to returns `404`, not `403`, so the API is not an
    existence oracle across orgs.
  contact:
    name: FuzeFront Platform Team
    url: https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront
  license:
    name: UNLICENSED

servers:
  - url: '{baseUrl}'
    description: >-
      Cluster-internal base URL. In the browser the shell always calls this
      service on a **same-origin** API base through the ingress — never a
      hard-coded absolute host (see CLAUDE.md).
    variables:
      baseUrl:
        default: http://fuzefront-selection-list-service:3011
        description: Base URL of the selection-list-service.

security:
  - bearerAuth: []

tags:
  - name: lists
    description: Selection lists — create, read, update, archive, purge.
  - name: items
    description: Items within a list — create, update, archive, purge, reorder.
  - name: translations
    description: Per-locale translations of lists and items, including machine autofill.
  - name: access
    description: Per-list access grants (ReBAC roles on the list instance).
  - name: quota
    description: Current quota usage and ceilings for the caller's organization.
  - name: resolve
    description: Hot path — cacheable bulk resolution of item ids to labels.

paths:
  /v1/selection-lists:
    get:
      operationId: listSelectionLists
      summary: List selection lists in the caller's organization
      description: >-
        Cursor-paginated. Scoped to the caller's organization and further
        filtered to the lists the caller can `read`; a list the caller has no
        grant on is simply absent, never a `403`. Each row carries its
        source-locale-resolved (or `locale`-resolved) `name`.
      tags: [lists]
      x-permit-action: read
      parameters:
        - name: limit
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Maximum rows to return. Clamped to `maximum` server-side — an
            over-max request is never honoured unbounded.
          schema:
            type: integer
            description: Page size.
            minimum: 1
            default: 50
            maximum: 200
        - name: cursor
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Opaque, server-issued cursor from the previous page's
            `page.nextCursor`. Echo it back unmodified; never construct or parse
            one. A malformed or expired cursor is a `400 VALIDATION_ERROR`,
            never a silent reset to page 1.
          schema:
            type: string
            description: Opaque pagination cursor.
            maxLength: 2048
        - name: status
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Filter lists by lifecycle status. Defaults to `active`.
          schema:
            type: string
            description: Lifecycle status filter.
            enum: [active, archived, all]
            default: active
        - name: locale
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Preferred locale for resolved text. Highest priority in the fallback
            chain; an unsupported value is a `400 VALIDATION_ERROR` rather than a
            silent fallback, so a client bug does not masquerade as missing
            translations.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Locale'
        - name: key
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Exact-match filter on the org-unique list `key`. Returns a page of at
            most one row; present so a consumer can look a list up by its stable
            slug without knowing its id.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionListKey'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of selection lists.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                description: A cursor-paginated page of selection lists.
                required: [items, page]
                additionalProperties: false
                properties:
                  items:
                    type: array
                    description: The selection lists on this page, newest first.
                    items:
                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionList'
                  page:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Page'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
    post:
      operationId: createSelectionList
      summary: Create a selection list
      description: >-
        Mints a `front_sl_`-prefixed id server-side; the body must not contain one.
        `key` must be unique within the organization (`409 CONFLICT` otherwise)
        and `name` seeds the `source_locale` translation. The caller is granted
        `list-owner` on the new list. Subject to the `org_lists` and `user_lists`
        quotas.
      tags: [lists]
      x-permit-action: add_value
      requestBody:
        required: true
        description: The list to create.
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionListCreate'
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The created selection list.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '409':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Conflict'

  /v1/selection-lists/{listId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ListIdParam'
    get:
      operationId: getSelectionList
      summary: Get one selection list
      description: >-
        Returns the list with its translation resolved through the locale
        fallback chain. Returns `404` — never `403` — when the caller cannot
        `read` it, so the endpoint is not a cross-org existence oracle.
      tags: [lists]
      x-permit-action: read
      parameters:
        - name: locale
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Preferred locale for resolved text. Highest priority in the fallback
            chain; an unsupported value is a `400 VALIDATION_ERROR` rather than a
            silent fallback, so a client bug does not masquerade as missing
            translations.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Locale'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The selection list.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionList'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
    patch:
      operationId: updateSelectionList
      summary: Update a selection list
      description: >-
        Partial update. Supplying `name`/`description` upserts the
        **`source_locale`** translation (marked `is_machine: false`) and
        invalidates the `source_hash` of every other locale, marking those
        translations stale for the next autofill. Changing `source_locale` does
        not re-translate anything.
      tags: [lists]
      x-permit-action: update
      requestBody:
        required: true
        description: The fields to change. Omitted fields are left untouched.
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionListUpdate'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The updated selection list.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '409':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Conflict'
    delete:
      operationId: deleteSelectionList
      summary: Archive (default) or purge a selection list
      description: >-
        Archives the list unless `purge=true`. Archiving is idempotent and
        reversible via `PATCH { "status": "active" }`; its items keep resolving.
        **Purging is irreversible**, cascades to every item, translation and
        access grant, and permanently breaks any consumer row still holding one
        of the purged item ids — which is why it requires `delete` (owner only)
        and an explicit opt-in rather than being the default verb.
      tags: [lists]
      x-permit-action: delete
      parameters:
        - name: purge
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            When `true`, permanently delete instead of archiving. Irreversible;
            breaks every consumer reference to the purged ids.
          schema:
            type: boolean
            description: Permanently delete rather than archive.
            default: false
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The archived list (only returned when `purge` is false/absent).
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionList'
        '204':
          description: The list was permanently purged. No body.
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'

  /v1/selection-lists/{listId}/archive:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ListIdParam'
    post:
      operationId: archiveSelectionList
      summary: Archive a selection list
      description: >-
        Sets `status` to `archived`. Idempotent — archiving an already-archived
        list returns `200` with the unchanged resource. The explicit verb exists
        so a UI need never call `DELETE` for the non-destructive outcome.
      tags: [lists]
      x-permit-action: delete
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The archived selection list.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SelectionList'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'

  /v1/selection-lists/{listId}/items:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ListIdParam'
    get:
      operationId: listSelectionListItems
      summary: List the items of a selection list
      description: >-
        Cursor-paginated, ordered by `sort_order` then `id`. Defaults to
        `status=active` — the set a picker should offer — so rendering a
        dropdown never accidentally offers archived choices. Pass
        `status=archived` or `status=all` to see the rest.
      tags: [items]
      x-permit-action: read
      parameters:
        - name: limit
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Maximum rows to return. Clamped to `maximum` server-side — an
            over-max request is never honoured unbounded.
          schema:
            type: integer
            description: Page size.
            minimum: 1
            default: 50
            maximum: 200
        - name: cursor
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Opaque, server-issued cursor from the previous page's
            `page.nextCursor`. Echo it back unmodified; never construct or parse
            one. A malformed or expired cursor is a `400 VALIDATION_ERROR`,
            never a silent reset to page 1.
          schema:
            type: string
            description: Opaque pagination cursor.
            maxLength: 2048
        - name: status
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Filter items by lifecycle status. Defaults to `active` so a picker
            never offers a retired choice by accident.
          schema:
            type: string
            description: Lifecycle status filter.
            enum: [active, archived, all]
            default: active
        - name: locale
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Preferred locale for resolved text. Highest priority in the fallback
            chain; an unsupported value is a `400 VALIDATION_ERROR` rather than a
            silent fallback, so a client bug does not masquerade as missing
            translations.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Locale'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of items, in `sort_order`.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                description: A cursor-paginated page of selection-list items.
                required: [items, page]
                additionalProperties: false
