ISSUE TITLE: Portal shows 10 of 19 products working: applications-service migrations 013/014 are not taking effect in prod after a redeploy
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
## Summary

The portal federation health census has failed on **every scheduled run** for at least six days. Current state (run [35820124167](https://github.com/izzywdev/FuzeFront/actions/runs/35820124167), 2026-09-23T04:53Z):

```
10 PASS, 7 FAIL, 4 MISSING (of 19 expected).
```

The census is working as designed — it is reporting real breakage, and nothing is acting on it.

This issue tracks the one cause that is **FuzeFront's own**, and inventories the rest so they can be routed to their owners.

---

## The FuzeFront-owned defect

**`applications-service` migrations 013 and 014 are not reflected in the production database, and a redeploy did not fix it.**

Two migration-specific predictions remain falsified against the live registry:

| Migration | Should have | Live reality (2026-09-23) |
|---|---|---|
| `013_suspend_stranded_duplicate_app_rows` | suspend the stranded `fuzesales` / `fuzeservice` duplicate rows | both still `activated` — **two products each render twice in the portal menu** |
| `014_clock_manifest_remoteentry_repair` | repair the Clock manifest to `/apps/clock/remoteEntry.js` | still `/apps/clock/assets/remoteEntry.js` → **HTTP 404** |

The census confirms both directly:

```
clock        Clock        activated  FAIL  .../apps/clock/assets/remoteEntry.js — HTTP 404
fuzesales    FuzeSales    activated  FAIL  fuzesales.prod.fuzefront.com/assets/remoteEntry.js — HTTP 404
sales        Sales        activated  PASS
fuzeservice  FuzeService  activated  PASS
service      Service      activated  FAIL  .../apps/service/remoteEntry.js — HTTP 404
```

plus the census's own roster warnings, which are the duplicate rows surfacing a second way:

```
##[warning]fuzeservice is in the registry but not in scripts/expected-portal-apps.json
##[warning]fuzesales is in the registry but not in scripts/expected-portal-apps.json
```

### Why "it's just a stale image" is no longer the explanation

On 2026-09-20 this looked like a frozen deployment: `/api/health` reported `uptime: 312636s` (≈3.6 days) with a Permit registration timestamp of `2026-09-16T17:28:32Z`, while four `release.yml` runs had succeeded and bumped the image tag in `values-prod.yaml` without rolling a pod.

**Prod has since redeployed** — `/api/health` now reports `uptime: 50398s` (≈0.58 days), booted `2026-09-22T19:55:33Z`. The migrations still have not taken effect. So this is not simply a stale image, and it needs a real root cause.

### Prime suspect, from the code

`backend/applications/src/index.ts:165-173`:

```ts
await waitForTable('organizations', 60, 2000)
await waitForTable('portals', 60, 2000)
await runMigrations(dbOptions)
```

`runMigrations` has **no `.catch`** — unlike `ensureBuiltins()` immediately below it, which is deliberately best-effort. So a throw here aborts startup. If the host backend's `portals` migration has not run, or any migration in the chain throws, the new pod crash-loops and **the old ReplicaSet keeps serving** — which reproduces exactly what we observe: a live service on old data, with `release.yml` green.

Note also the duplicated `011_` prefix in the migration directory (`011_apps_organization_id_not_null.ts` and `011_suspend_phantom_fuzequality_builtin.ts`). Knex orders lexicographically so this is not itself a bug, but it is worth confirming both are recorded as applied.

### Diagnostics needed (requires cluster access — not available from this repo)

```bash
kubectl -n fuzefront describe deploy applications-service        # is a new ReplicaSet stuck?
kubectl -n fuzefront get pods -l app=applications-service        # CrashLoopBackOff?
kubectl -n fuzefront logs deploy/applications-service --previous # did runMigrations throw?
argocd app get fuzefront                                         # sync status / last sync error
# and, against the applications DB:
select name from knex_migrations order by id desc limit 10;
```

### Ruled out (measured, 2026-09-20)

- **Chart defect** — `helm template` renders cleanly for `values.yaml` (18 resources) and `values-prod.yaml` (72); `kubeconform -ignore-missing-schemas` reports 69 valid / **0 invalid**.
- **Argo Application spec** — `deploy/argocd/applications/fuzefront.yaml` is correct: `automated` with `prune` + `selfHeal`, tracking `master`, `path: deploy/helm/fuzefront`, `values-prod.yaml`.
- **Release pipeline** — `release.yml` runs are green and do bump the image tag.
- **Migrations not wired to run** — they are: `index.ts:173` calls `runMigrations` on every boot.
- **Migration 011 being unsafe** — it was hardened on 2026-08-26 specifically to avoid a boot crashloop when the root org is absent.

---

## Not FuzeFront's — needs routing to owners

**Serving failures (5).** The registry row is correct; the product's own bundle does not serve:

| Slug | URL | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `fuzehub` | `/apps/fuzehub/remoteEntry.js` | 503 |
| `fuzeagent` | `/apps/fuzeagent/remoteEntry.js` | 503 |
| `picker` | `picker.prod.fuzefront.com/remoteEntry.js` | 503 |
| `contact` | `fuzecontact.prod.fuzefront.com/assets/remoteEntry.js` | 404 |
| `service` | `/apps/service/remoteEntry.js` | 404 — per migration 013's header, waits on izzywdev/FuzeService#84 |

Note `fuzeagent` is seeded from this repo's `BUILTIN_MANIFESTS`, but `values-prod.yaml`'s federated `upstreams` list contains only `fuzesocial`, so nothing in this chart serves `/apps/fuzeagent/`. Worth confirming which chart is expected to.

**Unregistered (4).** Nothing has ever written a registry row; each cause is documented in `scripts/expected-portal-apps.json` `_meta.genuinelyAbsentAtLastReview` and owned by the product's repo or FuzeInfra:

- `call` — FuzeInfra's one-time `argocd-register` has never run for izzywdev/FuzeCall; no namespace, no Ingress.
- `fuzex`, `fuzemerchandize` — Ingress exists but nothing healthy backs it (503), so the fail-closed init containers never complete.
- `plan` — its chart registers via a PostSync Job against the **legacy unauthenticated** `POST /api/apps/register`, which has required auth since appsec #100 and sets neither `slug` nor `manifest`. The Job swallows failures with `process.exit(0)`, so it reports Succeeded while never writing a row.

**Improved since 2026-09-20:** `fuzebi` now registers and passes (`10 PASS` vs `9`), and its display name is correctly de-prefixed to `BI`.

---

## Secondary: nobody is notified

The census has failed every ~6 hours for at least six days with no escalation. Whatever the root cause, a scheduled check that fails indefinitely into an empty room is its own defect. Worth deciding whether this should open/update an issue or page on sustained failure.

## Done means

- [ ] Root cause found for why 013/014 are not applied in prod, with evidence (pod state or `knex_migrations` contents)
- [ ] `clock` loads — census row PASS
- [ ] `fuzesales` and `fuzeservice` duplicate rows suspended; one tile per product
- [ ] Census `MISSING`/duplicate-warning rows for those two are gone
- [ ] Serving + unregistered failures routed to their owning repos (separate issues/delegations)
- [ ] A decision recorded on census failure escalation

